course: dictionary
lesson: 2594
title: Deodorant and growing up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deodorant is a substance you put under your arms. It stops or covers body smells caused by sweat.
explain: «During puberty, sweat glands become more active, so wash every day and use deodorant.» Puberty is the time when your body changes as you grow up. Your sweat glands work harder, so you may sweat more.
explain: The words around deodorant give you clues. «Around puberty special sweat glands in the armpits switch on; their sweat is not smelly until bacteria eat it, which is why a wash helps and why older children use deodorant.» Washing and deodorant go together: a wash helps, and deodorant covers any smell that is left.
fact: Deodorant is a noun: a deodorant, two deodorants. We also say deodorant on its own, as in «use deodorant».
fact: Common phrases are put on deodorant, roll-on deodorant and spray deodorant.
fact: «Deodorant» means a substance you put under your arms to stop or cover body smells caused by sweat.
fact: Sweat helps keep your body cool, but it can start to smell, so washing every day helps you stay fresh.
exercise: Where do you put deodorant? | On your knees | On your face | *Under your arms | In your shoes
exercise: Which phrase is used with deodorant? | Deodorant bed | Deodorant rain | Eat a deodorant | *Spray deodorant
exercise: Why do older children use deodorant? | To sleep better at night | To stop their shoes getting wet | *To stay fresh, because sweat can start to smell | To make their hair curly
test: «During puberty, sweat glands become more active, so wash every day and use deodorant.» What does deodorant do? | Makes you taller | Stops you feeling hungry | *Stops or covers body smells caused by sweat | Makes your sweat sweeter
test: Which word in the sentence tells you the time when your body changes as you grow up? | wash | *puberty | deodorant | every
exam: Why do washing and deodorant work well together? | *Washing helps keep smells down, and deodorant covers any smell that is left | Washing stops sweat completely, so deodorant is not needed | Washing is only for your hair, so deodorant does the rest | Washing makes you sweat more, so you need deodorant
